SOURCE OF TRUTH READ END-TO-END
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/src/features/admin/pages/TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx  — a thin PageContainer
  wrapper (title=featureConfig.title, subtitle=featureConfig.subtitle) around the
  shared <FeatureToggles/> component.
web/src/features/settings/components/FeatureToggles.tsx — the ACTUAL surface the
  page renders (the manifest extracted only the wrapper's 2 strings; FeatureToggles
  is NOT a separate parity unit, so it is implemented here to avoid a stub — ADR-011,
  Covenant #2). It reads useTeslaFeatureConfig() (GET /tesla/user/feature-config) +
  useRefreshTeslaFeatureConfig() (POST .../refresh), and renders one GlassPanel:
    - header: IconBox(Flag) + featureConfig.title + featureConfig.subtitle, plus the
      "Synced {formatDateTime(fetched_at)}" label + a Refresh button (spinner while
      pending; success/error toast → toast.featureConfigRefreshed/Failed).
    - body: a Feature / Status / Details grid (Badge success|neutral = Enabled|Disabled,
      details = the non-`enabled` object fields joined as "k: JSON.stringify(v)"),
      or the noData EmptyState when there are zero flags.
web/src/api/hooks/useUser.ts                            — TeslaConfigEnvelope { data,
  fetched_at }, the two hooks + their endpoints/toasts.
web/src/i18n/en.json (settings ns) + web/src/components/layout/Layout.tsx           —
  featureConfig.* defaults verbatim; the sidebar labels /tesla-features "Feature Flags"
  (purple flag) in the Account group.

