Both required strings render from the bound @Observable surface via the page chrome (web
PageContainer) and the panel header (web FeatureToggles header). Every other visible literal
also resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names — featureConfig.lastSynced/
refresh/feature/status/details/enabled/disabled/noData + toast.featureConfigRefreshed/Failed —
zero hardcoded UI literals (the #if DEBUG seed flag keys + "mtls"/region strings are sample
DATA the web renders un-i18n'd, not localizable chrome). The single data source (feature
config) implements all THREE required states + loaded: loading (TSTableSkeleton), empty (the
web noData ContentUnavailableView), error (TSErrorDisplay + Retry), loaded (the table). Refresh
maps the web mutation onSuccess/onError to a dismissible success/danger banner using the web
toast keys. SI converters: N/A (feature config carries no unit-bearing values; only the sync
timestamp formats at the boundary). a11y: page header + panel are combined a11y elements with
.isHeader titles; each table row is an a11y element with key label + Enabled/Disabled value;
Dynamic Type via Font.TS; light/dark/high-contrast via the design-token colors. Adaptive
macOS/iPad (columnar Grid) vs iPhone (per-row cards) via horizontalSizeClass (ADR-002/006).

