================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TeslaFeatureFlagsPage ships at parity with the web source. The
web page is a thin PageContainer around <FeatureToggles/>, and the native page reproduces that
1:1: a page header (title+subtitle from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names) above the
full Feature Toggles GlassPanel — icon header, "Synced …" timestamp, a Refresh action mapped to a
dismissible success/error banner, and a Feature/Status/Details table with Enabled/Disabled badges
— bound to an @Observable TeslaFeatureFlagsPageModel (P1/S8 — no networking in the view) that
owns the loading / empty / error / loaded states for the single feature-config source. A new
`.teslaFeatures` AppRoute (Account group, "tesla-features" segment, flag.checkered icon) +
TeslaFeatureFlagsRouteRegistration wire the page into the shell nav and the /tesla-features deep
link (executed routing harness 10/10). All on the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled
chrome, no web cloning). Verified GREEN by check-placeholders (0), swiftformat (0/9), swiftlint
--strict (0/9), isolated Swift 6 macOS + iOS type-checks (0 diagnostics), and the executed model
(36/36) + routing (10/10) harnesses. The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to a pre-existing,
out-of-scope `return`-in-ViewBuilder error in the untouched shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift —
